      "ed an important and useful role in the Gulf crisis, in trying to end the war in Afghanistan, and in opening the way for Arab-Israeli negotiations. We have been pleased to work with the Soviet leadership on these and other issues. The new leadership in Russia has assured us of their determination to continue this constructive role and has underscored that determination b",
      "for Israel's reasonable security needs. \" At the same time, we have consistently supported the legitimate rights of the Palestinian people and the principle of \"land for peace. \" In our view, this principle can be fulfilled without compromising Israel's security; indeed, I would even go SO far as to say that Israel's security stands to be enhanced by the peace process,"
