      "met with the King during his September visit to Washington; since then, several key issues have arisen: Lockerbie, the Middle East peace process, and the Algerian situation and its impact on the Western Sahara issue. Iraq is also a key concern. II. LOCKERBIE -- While we originally told the GOM we would understand if it took a neutral stance in the UNSC (so long as it did no",
      "reover, Venezuela's OPEC ties make it reluctant to offend the Arab World, and CAP fears pressure on Libya may aggravate Middle East tensions. He has suggested an international tribunal for terrorists. -- CAP has suggested elimination of the Permanent Five veto. Cuba and Central America -- CAP wants democratic reforms in Cuba but fears outside pressure could precipitate",
      "-- the attempted assassination of the Turkish Ambassador and an attempt to blow up a bus loaded with Jews emigrating to Israel from the former USSR in Budapest in December. Hungary has been an important transit point for Jews going to Israel and continues to welcome them despite threats and the recent bombing. V. IRAQ -- Hungary supported our efforts during Desert",
      "only. $4 million annually; funded from regular budget. 35 personnel. Indefinite mandate. Mid-East O UN Interim Force in Lebanon (UNIFIL). Established March 19, 1978 to confirm withdrawal of Israeli troops, restore peace, and assist the Government of Lebanon to restore effective authority in southern Lebanon. Peacekeepers. $75 million for a six-month period; funded"
