      "nal Arrangements: This third category of measures or arrangements would embrace all states of the Gulf and possibly the Middle East. In some ways, if the first category is analogous to NATO, and the second to COCOM, this would be the parallel to CSCE. It would include our friends in the region as well as Iraq, and Iran; it might also include Turkey, Egypt, SECRET 4 Syr",
      ". Second, U.S. relations with regional states (and in particular our ability to work with them) will be affected by the Arab-Israeli and Palestinian issues; without progress here, working relationships with Arabs everywhere will remain uneasy and unpredictable. We may deny linkage as a matter of policy, but we cannot ignore it as a fact of life. Moreover, and even were",
